`bt_cap_common_disconnected` will currently only mark the procedure as aborted, but if we do not get any notifications to trigger the final handling
```c
	if (bt_cap_common_proc_is_aborted()) {
		if (bt_cap_common_proc_all_handled()) {
			cap_initiator_unicast_audio_proc_complete();
		}

		return;
	}
```

of aborted proecedures, we end up in an aborted state. 

`bt_cap_common_disconnected` either needs to take that into account and finalize the abort for the CAP initiator (the CAP commander always use write requests), or the CAP initiator need to use write requests which require a change in the BAP Unicast client.
